From 00d8bbbc9c5c436ac7734f3c9c22081051f792ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:10:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gap-closing WIP: gate MTP shared-KV detection on the
 gemma4-assistant arch

A shared-NextN MTP head (nextn_shared_target_tensors, e.g. the qwen4exp
mtp-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-shared-Q8_0.gguf sidecar) ships no token_embd/output and
borrows the target's, so llama_init_from_model sets cparams.ctx_other = ctx_tgt
to satisfy the EAGLE3/DFLASH/QWEN4EXP tensor-sharing path.  The MTP draft driver
inferred is_mem_shared purely from ctx_other == ctx_tgt, so it took the gemma4
shared-KV arm: it re-added every draft token at the same position and skipped the
catch-up decode, and the second draft step died every round with

  init: ... last position ... X = N ... starting position Y = N
        for M-RoPE, it is required that the position satisfies: X < Y
  spec draft: llama_decode[1] returned -1

so a draft never exceeded one token and acceptance was ~0.

ctx_other is set for two different reasons; only gemma4-assistant actually shares
the target KV.  Gate is_mem_shared on the arch as well (the reference's fix).
Fixes the shared-NextN MTP head on qwen4exp: 0 errors, qwen4exp IQ4_NL +
shared-Q8_0 head acceptance 0.287 (acc per pos 0.679/0.462/0.333...), and the
adaptive path reports real depth transitions.

This is a delivery bug in block 01 (rdna-boosts has the same one-line inference);
it should be backported there.
---
 common/speculative.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/speculative.cpp b/common/speculative.cpp
index c711c30d0..145ffa9b1 100644
--- a/common/speculative.cpp
+++ b/common/speculative.cpp
@@ -1437,7 +1437,14 @@ struct common_speculative_impl_draft_mtp : public common_speculative_impl {
         llama_set_embeddings_nextn(ctx_tgt, true, /*masked*/ false);
         llama_set_embeddings_nextn(ctx_dft, true, /*masked*/ true);
 
-        is_mem_shared = llama_get_ctx_other(ctx_dft) == ctx_tgt;
+        // ctx_other is set for two different reasons: gemma4 assistants share the target KV, while
+        // qwen4exp/eagle3/dflash shared-NextN heads only borrow the target's token_embd/output
+        // (nextn_shared_target_tensors) and keep their own KV.  Only the former may reuse the target
+        // position for every draft token and skip the catch-up decode; gating on the arch (not just
+        // ctx_other) is what keeps a shared MTP head on the normal incrementing-position path.
+        char arch[64] = {0};
+        llama_model_meta_val_str(llama_get_model(ctx_dft), "general.architecture", arch, sizeof(arch));
+        is_mem_shared = llama_get_ctx_other(ctx_dft) == ctx_tgt && std::strcmp(arch, "gemma4-assistant") == 0;
         chain_heads   = n_mtp_layers > 1 && !is_mem_shared;
 
         // remember the user n_max: chain_heads caps it at the model MTP layer
